    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n101 Earlwood Estate is a well-located three-bedroom semi-detached home, ideally positioned on a generous south-west facing corner site in one of Cork's most sought-after residential areas, just a short stroll from The Lough.\n\nPresented in good decorative condition, the property is ready for immediate occupation, offering prospective purchasers an excellent opportunity to establish a home in a highly convenient and established location.\n\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall, living room, dining room, and kitchen at ground floor level. Upstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms and a family bathroom.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from a large gravel driveway providing ample off-street parking, with the added advantage of a detached garage offering valuable additional storage. The corner position further enhances the property's appeal, presenting excellent potential for extension, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nThe private, enclosed rear garden enjoys a sunny south-west orientation and is designed for low maintenance, featuring a patio area and level lawn. Pedestrian access is available via the garage.\n\nThe location is exceptionally convenient, within walking distance of The Lough, and in close proximity to CUH, UCC, Bon Secours Hospital, and Wilton Shopping Centre. Cork city centre is also easily accessible via regular public transport links and the nearby South Link Road network.\n\nThis is an excellent opportunity to acquire a turn-key home in a mature and highly desirable residential setting.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 4.75m x 2.36m\nThis bright and welcoming entrance hall features an original solid wood floor and under-stairs storage. The hall offers access to all ground floor accommodation.\n\nLiving Room - 3.63m x 4.35m\nThis spacious reception room overlooks the front garden and features a stone faced fireplace with tiled surround, built-in alcove storage, and wood flooring.\n\nDining Room - 3.61m x 3.59m\nReception room positioned to the rear of the home features wood flooring and an open fireplace. Built-in shelved alcove.\n\nKitchen - 3.62m x 3.15m\nFully fitted kitchen with built in eye and floor level units with appliances (cooker, fridge/freezer, dishwasher, washing machine), tiled splashback and tiled flooring. Provides direct access to the rear garden.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 3.11m x 3.18m\nThe landing opens to all bedrooms and the family bathroom. Hot press storage.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.60m x 3.62m\nLarge bright double bedroom to the front with wood flooring and built-in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.61m x 3.62m\nGenerous double bedroom which looks out over the rear garden features wood flooring and built-in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.51m x 3.15m\nSingle bedroom to the front features wood flooring and built-in wardrobes.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 1.63m x 3.19m\nPartially tiled four-piece bath suite with bath and separate shower. There is an electric shower fitting and a fitted storage cabinet.\n\n"
      },
